<title>UK: EIB prices April 2004 Eurobond.</title>
<headline>EIB prices April 2004 Eurobond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond has been priced, joint lead managers Caisse des Depots et Consignations, Paribas and SBC Warburg said.</p>
<p>The launch statement from the lead managers said: &quot;Until the start of such third stage (of EMU), all monetary rights and obligations in respect of the notes shall be deemed to be denominated in Ecu at the rate of one Ecu for one euro&quot;. The notes will be paid for in Ecu and coupons will be paid in Ecu until the introduction of the Euro, thereafter in euros.</p>
<p>+ + +</p>
<p> BORROWER   EUROPEAN INVESTMENT BANK</p>
<p> AMT    1.0 BLN ***   COUPON     5.25	MATURITY    15.APR.04</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  99.517    PAY DATE    14.FEB.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.875     REOFFER    97.942    SPREAD	+2 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA S&amp;P	  AAA</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 6.0 PCT 25.APR.04 ECU OAT</p>
<p> NOTES   ***FOR CURRENCY SEE TEXT ABOVE.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
